 "summary": "The canonical surface is minimal with hidden bodies: fiberCount, signSum, signCount, tarskiQuery, fullMatrix and fullInverse each carry their restatement, zero/empty, positivity, total-count and matrix-interaction lemmas with consistent simp/grind annotations, and the restricted-column recovery (mulVec_signCount, eq_signCount, solution_pos_iff over any CommRing K) closes the earlier gap. No compatibility artifacts, no Mathlib or in-repo duplicate (Mathlib has no fiber-count def or Tarski query), and the only private helpers are subtype-indexed expansions used solely within the file.",
